1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,700
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:16,970 --> 00:00:19,408
- She's arrived. - Okay.

3
00:00:22,763 --> 00:00:25,702
- Chungseong. - Chungseong.

4
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:28,330
I'm Major Kim Ha Na.

5
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:32,335
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin, the battalion commander. Please, sit.

6
00:00:40,430 --> 00:00:44,690
I've heard a lot about you from my colleague at the Corps Inspection Dept.

7
00:00:44,690 --> 00:00:48,483
I doubt you heard anything good. It wasn't flattering, was it?

8
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:52,510
I only heard good things.

9
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:54,370
That's strange.

10
00:00:55,461 --> 00:00:59,210
First, I apologize for visiting without prior notice.

11
00:00:59,210 --> 00:01:02,950
It's fine. So, what brings you here?

12
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:07,560
I'm here for a military-wide inventory audit.

13
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:10,514
For the next two days, we'll inspect each company's warehouses,

14
00:01:10,514 --> 00:01:13,856
equipment, and overall facilities.

15
00:01:15,190 --> 00:01:17,306
An inventory audit?

16
00:01:18,442 --> 00:01:20,795
[Inventory Audit]

17
00:01:21,874 --> 00:01:26,754
A Corps inspector, and a major at that,

18
00:01:26,754 --> 00:01:29,402
coming down for an inventory audit in person...

19
00:01:29,402 --> 00:01:30,970
seems a bit unusual.

20
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:35,950
It's proof that the higher-ups value this audit very much.

21
00:01:35,950 --> 00:01:39,266
Is that why you came by surprise?

22
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:44,934
I was worried you'd feel that way, so I called to give you a heads-up.

23
00:01:50,944 --> 00:01:53,183
But you didn't answer...

24
00:01:54,156 --> 00:01:55,323
sir?

25
00:01:57,670 --> 00:01:59,449
Is that so?

26
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:01,924
Major Kim Ha Na.

27
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:05,626
I'll leave the inventory audit in your hands.

28
00:02:05,626 --> 00:02:07,357
Thank you.

29
00:02:10,570 --> 00:02:11,998
Chungseong!

30
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:32,790
First Sergeant, you mean today?

31
00:02:32,790 --> 00:02:35,792
Yes, the Corps is conducting an inspection.

32
00:02:35,792 --> 00:02:37,730
[Final Ep. Sabotage]

33
00:02:37,730 --> 00:02:40,827
It doesn't seem like the right time for an inventory audit.

34
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:44,400
- First Sergeant, I've printed the ledgers. - Okay.

35
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:48,370
The numbers won't match anyway.

36
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:53,434
After roll call tomorrow, get the boys to flip the warehouses upside down.

37
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:00,070
If anything's missing, call other companies.

38
00:03:00,070 --> 00:03:03,890
- Major, I'll be waiting outside. - Alright.

39
00:03:05,836 --> 00:03:09,105
If all else fails, we'll just have to forge the ledgers.

40
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:11,733
- Right? - Yes, sir.

41
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:14,592
It's not like we haven't done this before.

42
00:03:18,657 --> 00:03:22,390
- Chungseong! - Chungseong! I'm Major Kim Ha Na.

43
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:25,289
I'm First Sergeant Park Jae Su, Second Company.

44
00:03:27,070 --> 00:03:30,127
The office is quite cluttered.

45
00:03:30,127 --> 00:03:32,037
Not at all.

46
00:03:32,037 --> 00:03:34,219
You've printed the property ledgers.

47
00:03:34,219 --> 00:03:38,050
- Uh, well. - You printed these for me, right? Thanks.

48
00:03:38,050 --> 00:03:41,930
I was going to organize them first...

49
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:48,520
Don't try to force the numbers to match by manipulating the ledgers.

50
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:52,732
And don't borrow missing items from other units.

51
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:55,983
What I hate most is forging documents.

52
00:03:55,983 --> 00:03:57,278
Yes, ma'am.

53
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:59,190
- First Sergeant? - Yes?

54
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:03,530
- Just show me everything transparently. - Yes, ma'am.

55
00:04:03,530 --> 00:04:06,710
- I'll leave it to you then. - Yes, ma'am.

56
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:08,943
- Chungseong! - Chungseong!

57
00:04:10,606 --> 00:04:12,111
Chungseong!

58
00:04:17,002 --> 00:04:20,694
She smiles, but says everything she wants to.

59
00:04:20,694 --> 00:04:23,865
If we forge anything, we're dead meat.

60
00:04:23,865 --> 00:04:28,471
Don't worry. The inventory audit, the inspection, the gear, the company...

61
00:04:28,471 --> 00:04:31,730
Let's just trust our veteran First Sergeant to handle it.

62
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:34,510
- Hey. - Yes, sir.

63
00:04:34,510 --> 00:04:37,760
- Want to see how trust can backfire? - I'd love to.

64
00:04:40,850 --> 00:04:42,616
- Let's clean up. - Yes, sir.

65
00:04:42,616 --> 00:04:44,576
- Why all of a sudden... - Knock it off, you punks.

66
00:04:44,576 --> 00:04:46,147
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

67
00:04:58,938 --> 00:05:00,710
Platoon Leader.

68
00:05:00,710 --> 00:05:01,830
Is it too early?

69
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:03,710
- Platoon Leader! - You scared me!

70
00:05:03,710 --> 00:05:05,574
What are you doing?

71
00:05:07,030 --> 00:05:11,555
A girl? Are you finally escaping your single life?

72
00:05:11,555 --> 00:05:14,250
Is it that obvious already?

73
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:17,670
- We're getting to know each other. - Is that so?

74
00:05:17,670 --> 00:05:21,113
She's quite a beauty. It's like a fated encounter.

75
00:05:21,113 --> 00:05:23,949
"A fated love."

76
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:26,770
- Even her name is charming. - Fated love.

77
00:05:26,770 --> 00:05:29,111
Kim Castro.

78
00:05:31,901 --> 00:05:33,610
Kim Castro?

79
00:05:33,610 --> 00:05:35,794
Do you know that name?

80
00:05:35,794 --> 00:05:38,254
Well, it's a big world, so it could be someone...

81
00:05:38,254 --> 00:05:40,190
Does she like Korea?

82
00:05:40,190 --> 00:05:42,662
Korea? Well, K-pop is popular these days.

83
00:05:42,662 --> 00:05:49,057
Did her parents die in a car accident when she was ten, leaving her all alone?

84
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:50,070
How did you know?

85
00:05:50,070 --> 00:05:53,353
And she can't video call due to security issues?

86
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:55,810
How do you know so much detail?

87
00:05:55,810 --> 00:06:00,110
Wait, Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu, did you date her too?

88
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:03,103
- She's scamming you. - She's seeing you?

89
00:06:03,103 --> 00:06:08,076
No, not seeing. Scamming. As in, she's a scammer.

90
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:10,646
A scam? My Castro would never do that.

91
00:06:10,646 --> 00:06:12,206
How can you be so sure?

92
00:06:12,206 --> 00:06:15,378
I was just like you at first, sir.

93
00:06:15,378 --> 00:06:19,862
- I almost got scammed too. - Almost?

94
00:06:20,964 --> 00:06:25,413
I thought the world would be waiting for me after my discharge.

95
00:06:25,413 --> 00:06:27,721
[5 Months Ago]

96
00:06:27,721 --> 00:06:32,638
But reality was very different from what I expected.

97
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:37,384
Hi.

98
00:06:37,384 --> 00:06:39,024
What's this?

99
00:06:39,024 --> 00:06:40,465
[Kim Castro]

100
00:06:41,751 --> 00:06:43,897
She's gorgeous.

101
00:06:48,705 --> 00:06:52,538
Hello.

102
00:06:52,538 --> 00:06:56,324
My name is Kim Castro from the United States.

103
00:06:56,324 --> 00:07:00,398
I'm currently deployed to Afghanistan.

104
00:07:00,398 --> 00:07:04,278
Your Korean is very good.

105
00:07:04,278 --> 00:07:06,551
My mother is Korean.

106
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:11,026
My parents died in a car accident when I was ten,

107
00:07:11,026 --> 00:07:13,683
and I was the only survivor.

108
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:18,396
So I became a soldier to become stronger.

109
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:23,652
I'll be your strength.

110
00:07:23,652 --> 00:07:28,490
Dear Il Gu, thank you so much.

111
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:30,492
"Dear..."

112
00:07:30,492 --> 00:07:33,902
After keeping in touch for a long time like that...

113
00:07:33,902 --> 00:07:37,541
Isn't this pretty much dating?

114
00:07:37,541 --> 00:07:43,463
Il Gu, I'm planning to leave the military and go to my mother's country, Korea.

115
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:46,909
I'll settle down there and live a normal life.

116
00:07:46,909 --> 00:07:51,354
Please come soon. I miss you.

117
00:07:52,514 --> 00:07:58,032
I miss you too, Il Gu. But I'm actually scared.

118
00:07:58,032 --> 00:08:00,741
I don't know anyone in Korea.

119
00:08:00,741 --> 00:08:05,277
I'll be all alone there.

120
00:08:05,277 --> 00:08:10,949
Don't worry. I'll be your guide.

121
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:15,196
I don't think I'll be lonely if you're there.

122
00:08:15,196 --> 00:08:17,831
But there's a problem.

123
00:08:17,831 --> 00:08:24,052
I need to book a flight, but I can't access my account from here.

124
00:08:24,052 --> 00:08:29,292
Can you send the money for the ticket to the booking agent for me?

125
00:08:29,292 --> 00:08:34,010
I'll pay you back as soon as I arrive.

126
00:08:35,318 --> 00:08:39,853
Wait, do I have enough money?

127
00:08:39,853 --> 00:08:44,678
Please help me just this once, my love.

128
00:08:44,678 --> 00:08:47,637
My balance is...

129
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:51,239
1,350 won.

130
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:55,558
I can't even afford the airport bus, let alone a plane ticket.

131
00:08:55,558 --> 00:08:58,581
I'm sorry, Castro.

132
00:08:58,581 --> 00:09:02,057
I haven't been paid for my part-time job yet.

133
00:09:02,057 --> 00:09:05,094
['Kim Castro' Cannot Be Found]

134
00:09:05,094 --> 00:09:09,716
What? Where did she go? Wait.

135
00:09:09,716 --> 00:09:13,344
Did I press something wrong? Or is it because she's deployed?

136
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:18,209
Right. The internet must be out there. She scared me.

137
00:09:18,209 --> 00:09:21,334
Kim Castro...

138
00:09:22,089 --> 00:09:26,618
[Rise in Romance Scams by Fake Overseas Female Soldiers]

139
00:09:26,618 --> 00:09:30,402
What? No way.

140
00:09:31,238 --> 00:09:34,910
It can't be. My love wouldn't do that.

141
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:37,078
Damn it!

142
00:09:37,078 --> 00:09:39,218
That bastard was a scammer!

143
00:09:39,218 --> 00:09:43,798
Damn it...

144
00:09:43,798 --> 00:09:48,038
I mean, I'm glad I didn't lose any money,

145
00:09:48,038 --> 00:09:50,458
but why do I feel so miserable?

146
00:09:50,458 --> 00:09:53,385
I was too poor to even get scammed.

147
00:09:53,385 --> 00:09:57,804
I thought I'd be able to date and go to school once I was discharged, but...

148
00:09:57,804 --> 00:10:01,518
I didn't even have money for food, let alone dating.

149
00:10:01,518 --> 00:10:03,551
Oh, dear.

150
00:10:05,998 --> 00:10:08,817
Tuition...

151
00:10:08,817 --> 00:10:13,298
At 4,580 won an hour, I'd only make a million won working my ass off all month.

152
00:10:13,298 --> 00:10:17,958
I worked to pay for school, but I couldn't go to school because I was always working.

153
00:10:17,958 --> 00:10:20,225
How tragic.

154
00:10:20,225 --> 00:10:21,892
But...

155
00:10:24,393 --> 00:10:26,879
[Army NCO Recruitment]

156
00:10:30,931 --> 00:10:33,758
Army NCO Recruitment.

157
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:37,038
Various welfare benefits.

158
00:10:37,038 --> 00:10:43,678
If I become a staff sergeant, I'll get food, a place to sleep, and a steady salary.

159
00:10:43,678 --> 00:10:46,398
And honestly, I miss the guys.

160
00:10:46,398 --> 00:10:49,816
If I'm an NCO, I can take better care of the guys too.

161
00:10:49,816 --> 00:10:52,358
Why not dedicate my youth one more time?

162
00:10:52,358 --> 00:10:54,838
This time, not for the country...

163
00:10:54,838 --> 00:10:56,998
But for my own livelihood.

164
00:10:56,998 --> 00:11:00,159
[Army NCO Recruitment] So that's why I applied.

165
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:03,958
Do you get it now? That Kim Castro is a total fraud.

166
00:11:03,958 --> 00:11:05,707
I see now.

167
00:11:05,707 --> 00:11:10,317
- Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu, let me hug you. - No, thank you.

168
00:11:10,317 --> 00:11:14,418
Anyway, Staff Sergeant Choi, it's clear you've been called by your country.

169
00:11:14,418 --> 00:11:19,578
Anyway, answer the country's call, but block that person immediately.

170
00:11:19,578 --> 00:11:21,021
I'll keep that in mind.

171
00:11:21,021 --> 00:11:24,578
But as your Platoon Leader, I was suspicious from the start.

172
00:11:24,578 --> 00:11:28,878
Giving your heart so easily is against a true soldier's spirit.

173
00:11:28,878 --> 00:11:32,898
Yes, well, I'm glad to hear that. I'll be on my way.

174
00:11:32,898 --> 00:11:35,431
Right, carry on.

175
00:11:38,691 --> 00:11:41,571
[Transfer 1,500,000 won to 'Kim Castro'?]

176
00:11:42,334 --> 00:11:43,334
[No]

177
00:11:46,318 --> 00:11:47,889
Thank goodness.

178
00:11:48,548 --> 00:11:50,980
[Block 'Kim Castro'?]

179
00:12:00,578 --> 00:12:05,358
When are we going to finish counting and organizing all this?

180
00:12:05,358 --> 00:12:08,990
We're out of time, so stop sighing and hurry up.

181
00:12:08,990 --> 00:12:10,896
I bet this won't match the ledger.

182
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:14,693
So don't just eyeball it. Count each one out loud.

183
00:12:14,693 --> 00:12:16,350
Don't make me do this twice. Got it?

184
00:12:16,350 --> 00:12:17,820
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

185
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:20,200
One. Two. Three, four.

186
00:12:22,210 --> 00:12:25,110
Kim Sang Hun, you too. You're not on your way out just yet.

187
00:12:25,110 --> 00:12:28,480
Yes, sir. Why are you so angry?

188
00:12:29,625 --> 00:12:31,187
- Corporal Park Min Seok. - Seven... huh?

189
00:12:31,187 --> 00:12:35,228
Do we count the blanket and the cover together as one set?

190
00:12:35,228 --> 00:12:39,300
No, you count them separately. There are no sets in the military.

191
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,090
Understood.

192
00:12:41,090 --> 00:12:44,411
- I lost count because of you! - I'm sorry.

193
00:12:45,656 --> 00:12:47,643
- Corporal Park Min Seok. - What now?

194
00:12:47,643 --> 00:12:51,104
- I can't find the covers. - Byeong Ho will bring them later.

195
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:52,706
- Gosh. - Understood.

196
00:12:52,706 --> 00:12:55,816
I lost count again! Just go over there and do something else.

197
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:57,835
Understood.

198
00:13:00,048 --> 00:13:01,855
Geez!

199
00:13:05,350 --> 00:13:07,870
- Hey, Kim Sang Hun. - Sergeant Kim Sang Hun.

200
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:09,902
Take the old mess tins with him

201
00:13:09,902 --> 00:13:11,667
- and write them off as lost. - Yes.

202
00:13:11,667 --> 00:13:15,810
While you're at it, take Moon Bit Na Ri and write him off too. Got it?

203
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:18,715
- Yes, Staff Sergeant. Da Hye. - Corporal Im Da Hye.

204
00:13:18,715 --> 00:13:21,884
Get the stuff to be discarded, and take Moon Bit Na Ri too.

205
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:24,429
- Yes, Sergeant. - Follow me, quick.

206
00:13:24,429 --> 00:13:26,573
I'll help too.

207
00:13:33,690 --> 00:13:35,260
Follow me.

208
00:13:36,050 --> 00:13:38,270
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu.

209
00:13:38,270 --> 00:13:40,069
Thank you for everything.

210
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:43,722
- Shut up and get lost! You're confusing me. - Understood.

211
00:13:43,722 --> 00:13:45,470
- Follow me, hurry. - Yes, sir.

212
00:13:45,470 --> 00:13:49,351
- Okay. Come on. - Yes, sir.

213
00:13:49,351 --> 00:13:50,925
Keep up the good work.

214
00:13:50,925 --> 00:13:54,625
- How many of these are there, Park Min Seok? - I forgot, sir.

215
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:58,130
Go help with the disposal. Follow them. Hurry up and get lost.

216
00:13:58,130 --> 00:14:00,787
13, all present.

217
00:14:02,259 --> 00:14:06,013
28, 29.

218
00:14:06,013 --> 00:14:08,565
30, 31.

219
00:14:08,565 --> 00:14:10,953
- 31? - Yes, that's correct.

220
00:14:10,953 --> 00:14:15,808
Man, it's tough without Sergeants Kang Chan Seok and Choi Byeong Nam.

221
00:14:15,808 --> 00:14:21,130
Tell me about it. Even if they were short-timers, they'd be some help...

222
00:14:21,130 --> 00:14:23,112
- Or would they? - Come on.

223
00:14:23,112 --> 00:14:25,630
I don't think they'd be any help at all.

224
00:14:25,630 --> 00:14:28,818
- Still, I kind of miss them. - Who?

225
00:14:28,818 --> 00:14:31,121
Those two civilians.

226
00:14:31,121 --> 00:14:32,956
You'd be dead.

227
00:14:32,956 --> 00:14:36,002
- Keep it up. - What's this?

228
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:40,289
Geez. What is all this?

229
00:14:40,289 --> 00:14:42,023
These are mess hall spoons.

230
00:14:42,023 --> 00:14:44,939
We have more than listed, so we have to write them off.

231
00:14:44,939 --> 00:14:48,889
- Why throw away perfectly good ones? - It's a problem if we're short.

232
00:14:48,889 --> 00:14:50,931
Can't we just keep extras?

233
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:52,830
Isn't it such a waste?

234
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:54,352
There's no other way.

235
00:14:54,352 --> 00:14:57,614
If we're short, it's a loss. If it's extra, it's embezzlement.

236
00:14:57,614 --> 00:15:01,733
The count must match the ledger exactly, down to the last digit.

237
00:15:01,733 --> 00:15:03,290
That's the military for you.

238
00:15:03,290 --> 00:15:06,590
But if you're tossing them, why are you bending them?

239
00:15:06,590 --> 00:15:10,990
We can't just toss them. We have to make them unusable.

240
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:14,519
So they can be discarded?

241
00:15:21,588 --> 00:15:23,676
I think my fingers are going to break.

242
00:15:23,676 --> 00:15:25,650
Look at this.

243
00:15:25,650 --> 00:15:28,850
A, B...

244
00:15:28,850 --> 00:15:32,830
C. And this one is D.

245
00:15:32,830 --> 00:15:35,517
He's doing it again. It's time for his meds.

246
00:15:35,517 --> 00:15:37,437
This guy is seriously out of his mind.

247
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:40,315
Alright, hang in there. We're almost done.

248
00:15:40,315 --> 00:15:42,734
Make me a D, please.

249
00:15:42,734 --> 00:15:48,295
Sergeant Kim, please stop! Sergeant Kim, stop with the spoons!

250
00:15:48,295 --> 00:15:50,032
What? What is it now?

251
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:55,622
- The mess hall is short 100 spoons. - What?

252
00:15:55,622 --> 00:15:59,793
They forgot to count the ones they lent to the other unit.

253
00:15:59,793 --> 00:16:02,495
So they need them back the way they were.

254
00:16:02,495 --> 00:16:05,690
How are we supposed to do that?

255
00:16:05,690 --> 00:16:08,521
Hey, straighten them all out.

256
00:16:08,521 --> 00:16:13,523
- Choi Jun Bae, that idiot. - What a waste.

257
00:16:13,523 --> 00:16:14,930
- Cha Byeong Ho. - Corporal Cha.

258
00:16:14,930 --> 00:16:16,263
Grab it.

259
00:16:16,263 --> 00:16:17,720
Stop me.

260
00:16:19,813 --> 00:16:21,507
I'll be on my way.

261
00:16:21,507 --> 00:16:23,097
Are you okay?

262
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:27,966
Master Sergeant Kim, it's me. How many canteens are left?

263
00:16:27,966 --> 00:16:30,489
Staff Sergeant Kim, any spare ski parka hoods?

264
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:32,758
Can we borrow about a hundred canteen covers?

265
00:16:32,758 --> 00:16:34,521
Come on, why be like this?

266
00:16:34,521 --> 00:16:37,829
We gave your unit a whole box of tent pegs last time.

267
00:16:37,829 --> 00:16:40,751
Do me a favor. I'll treat you at the hall this weekend, okay?

268
00:16:40,751 --> 00:16:44,986
Yes, our first sergeant will take the toughest job on the next project.

269
00:16:50,216 --> 00:16:51,730
Help me out here!

270
00:16:51,730 --> 00:16:54,154
- Communication security. Corporal No. - Do me a favor.

271
00:16:54,154 --> 00:16:57,417
I'll buy you coffee. When you guys go to training...

272
00:16:59,603 --> 00:17:02,093
- Chungseong! - I'm hanging up!

273
00:17:05,150 --> 00:17:07,819
The phones are ringing off the hook.

274
00:17:07,819 --> 00:17:10,430
Everyone must be busy because of the inventory audit.

275
00:17:10,430 --> 00:17:15,034
It's not like we're borrowing missing supplies from elsewhere.

276
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:18,288
It's "inter-unit cooperation."

277
00:17:18,288 --> 00:17:21,873
I clearly told you not to swap things around.

278
00:17:21,873 --> 00:17:25,002
Did you... forget already?

279
00:17:25,002 --> 00:17:27,317
It's not that...

280
00:17:27,317 --> 00:17:29,241
- First Sergeant. - Yes?

281
00:17:29,241 --> 00:17:34,679
My team just sealed the warehouses for the direct units and headquarters.

282
00:17:34,679 --> 00:17:39,550
There won't be a single canteen left, so don't waste your time calling.

283
00:17:39,550 --> 00:17:42,896
- Even the 1st Battalion down there... - There too.

284
00:17:42,896 --> 00:17:45,121
- The transport unit? - Yes, there too.

285
00:17:45,121 --> 00:17:48,694
- The recon unit? - Yes, all of them.

286
00:17:48,694 --> 00:17:53,230
I told you, it's a military-wide inventory audit. Carry on.

287
00:17:53,230 --> 00:17:56,399
- Yes. Chungseong. - Chungseong.

288
00:18:00,070 --> 00:18:04,827
First Sergeant, what now? Every possible source seems to be blocked.

289
00:18:06,570 --> 00:18:08,484
There's always a way.

290
00:18:09,110 --> 00:18:12,170
Have you ever heard of a canteen grave?

291
00:18:12,170 --> 00:18:14,657
A canteen grave?

292
00:18:22,311 --> 00:18:24,981
Kim Wan Soo, we don't need it.

293
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:30,132
This won't even dig in.

294
00:18:32,862 --> 00:18:37,701
From spoon duty to shovel duty. Damn it all.

295
00:18:38,424 --> 00:18:43,624
Does it even make sense that canteens are buried here?

296
00:18:43,624 --> 00:18:45,020
I don't know. Just dig.

297
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:49,079
Are you sure they're here? There's no end to this digging.

298
00:18:50,397 --> 00:18:52,664
- What's this? - Is it a canteen?

299
00:18:54,218 --> 00:18:56,678
It looks like a moldy blanket.

300
00:18:56,678 --> 00:19:01,850
I'm sure they buried it to fake the numbers, just like we do.

301
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:04,779
I hit something hard.

302
00:19:04,779 --> 00:19:06,200
What is it?

303
00:19:08,352 --> 00:19:11,152
What? What is this?

304
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:15,660
- Is this a time capsule? - Should I open it?

305
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:17,340
Open it.

306
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:20,988
It really is a time capsule.

307
00:19:23,926 --> 00:19:26,237
88 Light cigarettes!

308
00:19:26,237 --> 00:19:28,288
Shouldn't all of this be in a museum?

309
00:19:28,288 --> 00:19:32,213
When is this from? This Choco Pie design is so old-school.

310
00:19:32,213 --> 00:19:34,253
Look at the aura on these guys.

311
00:19:34,253 --> 00:19:35,420
Look at this.

312
00:19:35,420 --> 00:19:38,920
They look intense. Wait, aren't they North Korean spies?

313
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:43,200
- I'm so glad I wasn't in the army back then. - Seriously, what a relief.

314
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:47,181
Isn't this our first sergeant?

315
00:19:47,181 --> 00:19:48,941
You're right.

316
00:19:48,941 --> 00:19:54,060
First Sergeant, he looked exactly like a North Korean spy back then.

317
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:57,600
- I'll keep this safe. - Keep it safe.

318
00:19:58,420 --> 00:20:00,354
Let's keep digging.

319
00:20:01,034 --> 00:20:03,828
- I found them! I found them! - You did?

320
00:20:03,828 --> 00:20:05,135
There really are canteens.

321
00:20:05,135 --> 00:20:07,163
Hurry and dig out a hundred.

322
00:20:12,378 --> 00:20:14,556
There are mess kits too.

323
00:20:14,556 --> 00:20:17,916
- Corporal Kim Dong Woo, a helmet! - Hey, this is...

324
00:20:17,916 --> 00:20:19,511
What is all this?

325
00:20:19,511 --> 00:20:23,667
We have enough gear to start a whole new unit.

326
00:20:23,667 --> 00:20:27,379
I found some tent pegs here.

327
00:20:27,379 --> 00:20:29,000
Nice, good job.

328
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,495
Corporal Kim Dong Woo, are we taking it all?

329
00:20:31,495 --> 00:20:32,563
No.

330
00:20:32,563 --> 00:20:37,220
No. Let's just take a hundred and bury the rest again.

331
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:39,201
We're just burying them?

332
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:42,475
We have to think of our descendants too.

333
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:45,280
What a deep thought.

334
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:47,120
- Let's hurry up. - Yes, sir.

335
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:49,440
- Let's go, let's go. - There are two more here.

336
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:53,300
- Man, this is tiring. - Another one! Another one!

337
00:20:53,300 --> 00:20:56,360
A mess kit!

338
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:58,965
One wrong move and this could collapse.

339
00:20:58,965 --> 00:21:01,547
- Take a photo over there. - Yes, ma'am.

340
00:21:17,986 --> 00:21:20,303
This is serious.

341
00:21:25,980 --> 00:21:29,233
Major Kim Ha Na, here you are.

342
00:21:29,233 --> 00:21:31,526
- Chungseong. - Chungseong.

343
00:21:33,370 --> 00:21:35,170
It's quite worn out, isn't it?

344
00:21:35,170 --> 00:21:39,508
Yes, Battalion Commander. The building seems very old.

345
00:21:39,508 --> 00:21:41,420
Indeed.

346
00:21:41,420 --> 00:21:47,680
But you're checking cracks like a facility officer instead of an inspector.

347
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:49,920
Do you usually check things like this?

348
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:52,124
Buildings are also military assets.

349
00:21:52,124 --> 00:21:55,161
I'll be on my way then. Chungseong.

350
00:21:55,161 --> 00:21:56,567
Chungseong.

351
00:22:12,376 --> 00:22:15,040
Fragmentation grenades.

352
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:17,420
No issues.

353
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:21,420
- Next, 5.56mm ball ammunition. Report. - No issues.

354
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:24,840
- Good. Next, tracers. - No issues.

355
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:25,932
Excellent.

356
00:22:25,932 --> 00:22:30,680
The essence of ammo management is accuracy without a single round of error.

357
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:33,658
Next, blanks.

358
00:22:40,235 --> 00:22:44,128
The essence of ammo management is accuracy without a single round of error.

359
00:22:51,056 --> 00:22:53,634
Why are these blanks just left here?

360
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:55,700
I'm not sure, sir.

361
00:22:55,700 --> 00:22:58,085
The ledger says we don't have any left.

362
00:22:58,085 --> 00:23:02,680
This is a serious matter that could shake the entire ammo management system.

363
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:06,380
So I've prepared the blank firing adapter and the K-2 rifle.

364
00:23:06,380 --> 00:23:08,260
- Sergeant Kim Sang Hun. - Sergeant Kim Sang Hun!

365
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:12,182
I highly commend your initiative in anticipating and preparing for this.

366
00:23:12,182 --> 00:23:14,143
- Thank you, sir. - However,

367
00:23:14,143 --> 00:23:16,645
a soldier must always follow rules and procedures.

368
00:23:16,645 --> 00:23:20,292
As Platoon Leader, I'll see the ammo officer and get official instructions.

369
00:23:20,292 --> 00:23:22,600
You men, wait here for a moment. Understood?

370
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:24,654
- Yes, sir! - Chungseong! Love you!

371
00:23:24,654 --> 00:23:26,077
Love you too.

372
00:23:27,587 --> 00:23:29,247
What's all this?

373
00:23:29,247 --> 00:23:33,374
Sergeant Kim, isn't it better to have extra ammo than to be short?

374
00:23:33,374 --> 00:23:35,360
We can just use the leftovers later.

375
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:37,707
You're being clueless again, you idiot.

376
00:23:37,707 --> 00:23:42,560
If we have leftover training ammo, the higher-ups will think we didn't train.

377
00:23:42,560 --> 00:23:47,040
If we're flagged for poor training, everyone from the battalion commander down is screwed.

378
00:23:47,040 --> 00:23:52,840
But if the count doesn't match the ledger, won't we get disciplined?

379
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:55,684
That's why I brought the rifle, dummy.

380
00:23:55,684 --> 00:23:59,254
We'll just put on the adapter and fire them all off.

381
00:23:59,254 --> 00:24:01,954
Oh, I see.

382
00:24:04,444 --> 00:24:06,304
Close it, close it!

383
00:24:06,304 --> 00:24:07,981
Chungseong!

384
00:24:09,157 --> 00:24:10,833
You have a lot of ammo left?

385
00:24:10,833 --> 00:24:14,295
- Well... - That means you didn't train enough.

386
00:24:14,295 --> 00:24:16,331
- It's not that... - Where's the platoon leader?

387
00:24:16,331 --> 00:24:18,616
He went to see the ammo officer.

388
00:24:18,616 --> 00:24:23,100
- To discuss how to handle this? - No, ma'am.

389
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:26,080
- Grab the ammo boxes and mags and follow me. - Come again?

390
00:24:26,080 --> 00:24:29,386
- I said follow me. - Yes, ma'am!

391
00:24:29,386 --> 00:24:34,433
The log says you used it all, so you must have falsified it.

392
00:24:34,433 --> 00:24:38,940
- Well... - Hiding ammo and false reporting.

393
00:24:38,940 --> 00:24:41,563
This won't end with the platoon leader.

394
00:24:41,563 --> 00:24:44,893
The battalion commander could be disciplined.

395
00:24:46,653 --> 00:24:49,239
- Take this. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri!

396
00:24:49,239 --> 00:24:51,621
- The rifle. - Come again?

397
00:24:51,621 --> 00:24:53,546
I said give me the rifle.

398
00:24:55,180 --> 00:24:59,103
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun. Weapon number 210782.

399
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:02,180
The magazine.

400
00:25:02,180 --> 00:25:04,153
Corporal Im Da Hye!

401
00:25:21,456 --> 00:25:23,667
- Give it to me. - Yes, ma'am.

402
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:43,840
Take this.

403
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:47,087
I've shot the blanks. On to the next.

404
00:25:47,087 --> 00:25:49,198
You mean...

405
00:25:59,309 --> 00:26:01,006
Is this a memorial service?

406
00:26:01,006 --> 00:26:06,230
- Why aren't you eating? Dig in. - Yes, ma'am!

407
00:26:21,914 --> 00:26:25,169
This inventory audit is brutal.

408
00:26:25,933 --> 00:26:28,037
Chungseong!

409
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:32,220
- Hey, good job. Come and eat. - Come again?

410
00:26:32,220 --> 00:26:35,142
Dong Woo, you won't believe it,

411
00:26:35,142 --> 00:26:38,807
but the inspector bought all of these.

412
00:26:38,807 --> 00:26:41,400
- The inspector did? - Yes.

413
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:44,080
Is it okay for us to eat this?

414
00:26:44,080 --> 00:26:47,320
- Just come here and eat. - Yes, ma'am. Thank you!

415
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:49,128
- Thank you. - Thank you.

416
00:26:51,862 --> 00:26:55,608
- I was so hungry. Thank you for the food. - Sure.

417
00:26:58,140 --> 00:27:02,944
I've never actually talked to an inspector like this in my entire military career.

418
00:27:02,944 --> 00:27:04,480
It's pretty cool.

419
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:08,587
I'm pretty cool, right? I think so too.

420
00:27:08,587 --> 00:27:13,200
You're the most beautiful female officer I've ever met.

421
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:16,340
- I wish you'd visit our unit more often. - All right, I get it.

422
00:27:16,340 --> 00:27:22,479
When you were firing those shots earlier, you looked so incredibly charismatic.

423
00:27:22,479 --> 00:27:26,071
I'm better at buying PX food than shooting.

424
00:27:27,981 --> 00:27:31,466
- Eat up. - Yes, thank you.

425
00:27:33,111 --> 00:27:39,520
I've been watching you all, and you're quite a talented bunch.

426
00:27:39,520 --> 00:27:43,600
- Who's the biggest ace here? - That would be Sergeant Kim Sang Hun.

427
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:46,240
- Hey, Hyeon Uk is an ace too. - That's true.

428
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:49,042
Corporal Kim Dong Woo's muscles are insane.

429
00:27:49,042 --> 00:27:52,820
Plus, he's got a soft, gentle face.

430
00:27:52,820 --> 00:27:57,620
You guys would do great in the Special Forces or Reconnaissance. Right?

431
00:27:57,620 --> 00:28:00,020
- That's right. - Yes, ma'am.

432
00:28:00,020 --> 00:28:04,141
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri! I'm often told I'd fit right in the Marines!

433
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:06,566
- Really? - ♪ Red Beret ♪

434
00:28:06,566 --> 00:28:09,189
- Hey, knock it off. - Shut up, you idiot.

435
00:28:09,189 --> 00:28:11,169
- Yes, sir. - Sorry, ma'am.

436
00:28:12,900 --> 00:28:16,764
- Hurry up and eat. - Thank you.

437
00:28:29,592 --> 00:28:32,921
You all worked very hard during the inventory audit.

438
00:28:32,921 --> 00:28:37,382
And this is the report on the garrison's deterioration, graded D for aging,

439
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:42,069
and the results of a multifaceted evaluation of unit operational efficiency.

440
00:28:47,936 --> 00:28:49,533
Thank you.

441
00:28:54,443 --> 00:29:00,415
[Unit Consolidation Due Diligence Report]

442
00:29:04,273 --> 00:29:06,494
[13th Corps Inspection Department]

443
00:29:17,520 --> 00:29:19,210
Major Kim Ha Na.

444
00:29:19,980 --> 00:29:22,140
What is this?

445
00:29:22,140 --> 00:29:24,804
This investigation wasn't just a simple inventory audit.

446
00:29:24,804 --> 00:29:29,680
It was a due diligence review to select units for consolidation due to troop reduction.

447
00:29:29,680 --> 00:29:31,728
- Does that mean... - Yes.

448
00:29:31,728 --> 00:29:35,357
Shinhwa Unit has been finalized as a unit for consolidation,

449
00:29:35,357 --> 00:29:40,335
and the current garrison will be closed once the reorganization is complete.

450
00:29:41,032 --> 00:29:43,027
Wait, what are you talking about?

451
00:29:45,060 --> 00:29:46,520
It means the unit...

452
00:29:47,871 --> 00:29:50,105
is being disbanded.

453
00:29:50,740 --> 00:29:52,544
Yes, that's correct.

454
00:29:59,386 --> 00:30:02,499
[Finalized as a Unit for Consolidation]

455
00:30:17,401 --> 00:30:19,887
[Finalized as a Unit for Consolidation]

456
00:30:21,980 --> 00:30:24,366
It's not like this was my decision.

457
00:30:24,366 --> 00:30:27,200
I hope you understand that the decision to disband

458
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:31,200
was based on troop reduction and the state of aging units.

459
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:33,860
Then what happens from here?

460
00:30:33,860 --> 00:30:36,253
The division commander's been briefed.

461
00:30:36,253 --> 00:30:39,885
Now that the due diligence, inventory check, and facility surveys are finished,

462
00:30:39,885 --> 00:30:45,020
troop reassignment will begin as soon as the equipment transfer plan is finalized.

463
00:30:45,020 --> 00:30:48,574
I expect it will still take a few months.

464
00:30:51,185 --> 00:30:53,780
I wondered why you showed up so suddenly.

465
00:30:53,780 --> 00:30:56,415
I never imagined it was for consolidation.

466
00:30:56,415 --> 00:30:58,940
You really fooled me completely.

467
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:03,100
- I didn't fool you. I just told you late. - Isn't that the same thing?

468
00:31:03,100 --> 00:31:05,303
I was just doing as I was told.

469
00:31:05,303 --> 00:31:08,637
If it were announced before the inspection, it'd be awkward for me as the inspector.

470
00:31:08,637 --> 00:31:13,594
It's better to be awkward once at the end than to be awkward the whole time.

471
00:31:15,720 --> 00:31:18,233
- Are you okay? - Yes.

472
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:23,760
I think the Second Company Commander is the most shocked.

473
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:27,360
I'm fine. It's just so unexpected.

474
00:31:27,360 --> 00:31:30,555
I mean, disbanding this unit...

475
00:31:30,555 --> 00:31:35,741
With local community issues and all, it won't be a simple task.

476
00:31:35,741 --> 00:31:39,932
As times change, the military must change as well.

477
00:31:40,620 --> 00:31:42,027
It's truly a shame.

478
00:31:42,027 --> 00:31:46,865
Why is the mood like this? I feel like the bad guy here.

479
00:31:46,865 --> 00:31:51,722
- It's not just a feeling. - What can we do? Orders are orders.

480
00:31:52,360 --> 00:31:54,560
When will you notify the soldiers?

481
00:31:54,560 --> 00:31:57,860
Shouldn't we tell them right away?

482
00:31:57,860 --> 00:32:01,253
They probably already know by now.

483
00:32:01,253 --> 00:32:03,100
Already?

484
00:32:03,100 --> 00:32:06,760
The unit's being disbanded! Huge news!

485
00:32:06,760 --> 00:32:08,780
You have amazing instincts.

486
00:32:08,780 --> 00:32:10,650
- Right? I knew something was up. - Yes, sir.

487
00:32:10,650 --> 00:32:13,008
- Let's go, hurry up! - Yes, sir.

488
00:32:15,102 --> 00:32:17,896
Oddly, news travels fast in the Second Company.

489
00:32:17,896 --> 00:32:19,800
We have a "bat" living in our company.

490
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:23,820
Yes. That bat is active even during the day.

491
00:32:23,820 --> 00:32:26,020
- Huge news! Huge news! - Huge news!

492
00:32:26,020 --> 00:32:27,940
Want to hear? Multipurpose room!

493
00:32:27,940 --> 00:32:30,035
- Multipurpose room, now! - I'm coming!

494
00:32:30,035 --> 00:32:33,535
- Huge news! Hurry up, hurry up! - Huge news!

495
00:32:33,535 --> 00:32:35,520
When is Major Kim Ha Na returning?

496
00:32:35,520 --> 00:32:37,963
I'll be returning immediately.

497
00:32:44,900 --> 00:32:46,533
This...

498
00:32:47,319 --> 00:32:50,346
[Battalion Commander's Office]

499
00:32:50,980 --> 00:32:54,360
Yes. The official word on the disbandment just came out.

500
00:32:54,360 --> 00:32:56,680
Yes, that's right.

501
00:32:56,680 --> 00:33:00,783
Everyone was surprised, but they seemed calmer than expected.

502
00:33:00,783 --> 00:33:03,564
[The Day Before the Inspection]

503
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:14,326
I was worried you'd feel that way, so I called to give you a heads-up.

504
00:33:14,326 --> 00:33:16,600
But you didn't answer.

505
00:33:16,600 --> 00:33:19,286
Yes. I'll report back. Chungseong!

506
00:33:27,216 --> 00:33:30,800
Battalion closure. Battalion Commander Byeon Hyeok Jin.

507
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:33,135
That's not enough of a disgrace.

508
00:33:33,135 --> 00:33:35,940
Let's take it slow.

509
00:33:35,940 --> 00:33:38,660
It's only a matter of time anyway.

510
00:33:38,660 --> 00:33:41,018
After the unit, it's the people, right?

511
00:33:41,018 --> 00:33:42,953
Cho Baek Ho.

512
00:33:42,953 --> 00:33:45,594
Byeon Hyeok Jin, and...

513
00:33:46,485 --> 00:33:48,779
Major General Park Chun Gyu.

514
00:33:48,779 --> 00:33:52,948
It's a shame we couldn't move faster.

515
00:33:52,948 --> 00:33:54,580
Just wait a little longer.

516
00:33:54,580 --> 00:33:58,660
If it weren't for that Major General Park Chun Gyu...

517
00:33:58,660 --> 00:34:04,409
I would've gotten a star already. He's an obstacle to my career.

518
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:10,719
Don't worry. That obstacle will disappear soon.

519
00:34:11,340 --> 00:34:13,785
Even the annoying ones.

520
00:34:17,306 --> 00:34:20,440
- Corporal Kim Dong Woo, did you hear? - Hear what?

521
00:34:20,440 --> 00:34:23,520
- That our unit is being disbanded. - Are you sure?

522
00:34:23,520 --> 00:34:25,940
Corporal No said it's big news.

523
00:34:25,940 --> 00:34:28,120
Well, I heard it too.

524
00:34:28,120 --> 00:34:30,540
But can a unit be disbanded so easily?

525
00:34:30,540 --> 00:34:33,240
If it really happens, what becomes of us?

526
00:34:33,240 --> 00:34:38,140
- What else? Early discharge. - Really?

527
00:34:38,140 --> 00:34:40,980
- As if. - Chungseong!

528
00:34:40,980 --> 00:34:44,940
- Love you, sir. - Not many days left to love me.

529
00:34:44,940 --> 00:34:48,505
- Is it true the unit is being disbanded? - Seems like it.

530
00:34:48,505 --> 00:34:51,631
But it won't happen immediately. There's a process.

531
00:34:51,631 --> 00:34:53,400
But why is it being disbanded?

532
00:34:53,400 --> 00:34:55,468
There aren't enough people.

533
00:34:55,468 --> 00:34:59,420
I heard it's due to the reduction in military forces.

534
00:34:59,420 --> 00:35:01,185
Then where do we go?

535
00:35:01,185 --> 00:35:04,348
I don't know. I don't even know my own future.

536
00:35:04,348 --> 00:35:07,527
I'd like to know where I'm going too.

537
00:35:07,527 --> 00:35:10,960
- Out of my way. - Take care, sir.

538
00:35:10,960 --> 00:35:14,040
- I don't want to part ways. - It's okay, Jeong Min. Stop lying.

539
00:35:14,040 --> 00:35:16,288
I'm serious, sir.

540
00:35:21,020 --> 00:35:23,080
- Min Seok. - Corporal Park Min Seok.

541
00:35:23,080 --> 00:35:26,340
- Did you hear anything from your father? - Not a single thing, sir.

542
00:35:26,340 --> 00:35:28,400
- Hey, attention. - Attention!

543
00:35:28,400 --> 00:35:31,173
- Is everyone here? - Yes, sir.

544
00:35:31,173 --> 00:35:35,140
- You know why I called you here, right? - Yes, sir.

545
00:35:36,160 --> 00:35:39,360
- Surprised? - Yes, sir.

546
00:35:39,360 --> 00:35:41,896
I was surprised too.

547
00:35:41,896 --> 00:35:45,460
You've heard the rumors, and that's how it is.

548
00:35:45,460 --> 00:35:49,280
Per the Ministry of National Defense policy due to the reduction in forces...

549
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:51,686
it's been decided to disband the unit.

550
00:35:53,740 --> 00:35:57,863
Things will be chaotic for a while, so follow orders well. Got it?

551
00:35:57,863 --> 00:35:59,725
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

552
00:36:01,360 --> 00:36:06,600
I'll take questions so you don't believe the nonsense going around. Any questions?

553
00:36:06,600 --> 00:36:08,460
- Sergeant Kim Sang Hun. - Sang Hun.

554
00:36:08,460 --> 00:36:12,760
Will we all be split up? Or will we stay together?

555
00:36:12,760 --> 00:36:17,400
We'll know once the reassignment starts. Just wait a bit.

556
00:36:17,400 --> 00:36:18,977
Yes, sir.

557
00:36:20,860 --> 00:36:25,240
Corporal Kim Dong Woo. What happens to you, Company Commander?

558
00:36:25,240 --> 00:36:27,600
I don't know that either.

559
00:36:27,600 --> 00:36:30,946
- Why? Do you want to come with me? - Yes, sir.

560
00:36:30,946 --> 00:36:33,254
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

561
00:36:34,194 --> 00:36:37,800
I appreciate the sentiment, you guys.

562
00:36:37,800 --> 00:36:39,825
- Corporal Ji Jeong Min. - Yes.

563
00:36:39,825 --> 00:36:41,720
Then which unit are we going to?

564
00:36:41,720 --> 00:36:45,260
It's not certain, but I've heard it's either a GOP division...

565
00:36:45,260 --> 00:36:49,579
or the Air Defense Brigade, famous for being a mountain unit.

566
00:36:50,620 --> 00:36:51,740
Air Defense?

567
00:36:51,740 --> 00:36:54,838
Corporal Park Min Seok, where is the GOP?

568
00:36:54,838 --> 00:36:59,607
You stand guard right in front of the North.

569
00:37:00,600 --> 00:37:04,651
The first sergeant will take your preferences for the new units later.

570
00:37:04,651 --> 00:37:05,890
Of course...

571
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:09,980
You won't all get what you want, but they'll try to accommodate us.

572
00:37:09,980 --> 00:37:13,373
Tell the guys to choose wisely.

573
00:37:13,373 --> 00:37:18,121
[Survey of Reassignment Preferences Due to Unit Consolidation]

574
00:37:18,121 --> 00:37:21,742
First Sergeant, is staying behind an option too?

575
00:37:21,742 --> 00:37:25,704
Even if the people leave, the building stays, so someone has to maintain it.

576
00:37:25,704 --> 00:37:27,200
Sounds nice.

577
00:37:27,200 --> 00:37:29,513
We'll see if it's sweet or not.

578
00:37:29,513 --> 00:37:33,968
- Anyway, tell them to check carefully. Got it? - Yes, sir.

579
00:37:33,968 --> 00:37:37,508
Dong Woo, isn't it better to move than to stay behind?

580
00:37:37,508 --> 00:37:40,594
- The Air Defense Brigade sounds okay. - That's true.

581
00:37:40,594 --> 00:37:42,051
First of all...

582
00:37:42,051 --> 00:37:43,138
Sung Yoon Mo.

583
00:37:43,138 --> 00:37:45,460
- Corporal Sung Yoon Mo. - What about you?

584
00:37:45,460 --> 00:37:50,060
- I want to share my fate with you, sir. - Fate, my foot.

585
00:37:50,060 --> 00:37:54,151
- I'll follow you, sir. - But I don't like you.

586
00:37:57,020 --> 00:37:59,886
- Get back to work, you punk. - Yes, sir.

587
00:38:06,119 --> 00:38:09,880
Are we really all going to be split up based on what we check here?

588
00:38:09,880 --> 00:38:13,218
I don't know. Nothing is certain.

589
00:38:18,173 --> 00:38:20,382
You're back.

590
00:38:20,382 --> 00:38:22,942
Chungseong! Love you!

591
00:38:22,942 --> 00:38:27,015
Private Kim Hyeon Uk. I've returned to Barracks 1 after my leave.

592
00:38:27,015 --> 00:38:30,448
Reporting for duty. Chungseong!

593
00:38:33,440 --> 00:38:34,800
What's with your hair?

594
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:40,300
I tried to trim it myself on leave, but I messed it up, so I just shaved it all.

595
00:38:40,300 --> 00:38:43,002
- It suits you. - Thank you.

596
00:38:43,002 --> 00:38:45,680
- I'm so damn jealous. - Of my hair?

597
00:38:45,680 --> 00:38:47,760
Of your leave, man.

598
00:38:47,760 --> 00:38:51,621
Well, I tried cutting it myself, and it was actually kind of fun.

599
00:38:51,621 --> 00:38:55,300
I'll learn some barbering skills and take care of my seniors' hair from now on.

600
00:38:55,300 --> 00:38:58,751
Sure, I'm rooting for you. Unpack.

601
00:38:58,751 --> 00:39:00,283
Yes, sir.

602
00:39:09,120 --> 00:39:12,443
Did something happen while I was gone?

603
00:39:12,443 --> 00:39:14,260
Don't be shocked.

604
00:39:14,260 --> 00:39:17,740
- Yes, sir. - Our unit is being disbanded.

605
00:39:17,740 --> 00:39:21,640
- The unit is being disbanded? - Take a look at this.

606
00:39:21,640 --> 00:39:23,126
Thank you.

607
00:39:31,180 --> 00:39:33,100
Stop peeking.

608
00:39:33,100 --> 00:39:35,558
I can't see it.

609
00:39:55,160 --> 00:39:57,900
Are you checking "remain at unit?"

610
00:39:57,900 --> 00:40:00,020
I think that'll be the most popular choice.

611
00:40:00,020 --> 00:40:03,654
Staying at the original base will probably be the top pick.

612
00:40:03,654 --> 00:40:05,860
What do the people who stay behind do?

613
00:40:05,860 --> 00:40:09,095
I heard they just pull guard duty. But think about it.

614
00:40:09,095 --> 00:40:13,202
If everyone else leaves, the few left will have a hellish guard schedule.

615
00:40:13,202 --> 00:40:15,832
What about the GOP? I saw it on TV a lot.

616
00:40:15,832 --> 00:40:20,295
I heard from my friends that since it's the front line, the facilities are great.

617
00:40:20,295 --> 00:40:24,755
And since you only do guard duty, there's no training, and you get lots of leave.

618
00:40:24,755 --> 00:40:26,783
The food is amazing too.

619
00:40:26,783 --> 00:40:28,440
Really?

620
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:34,900
And since there are only a few dozen people, not hundreds, they're very close.

621
00:40:34,900 --> 00:40:37,300
Do you know why?

622
00:40:37,300 --> 00:40:40,899
Isn't it because they're stuck together and form a tight bond?

623
00:40:40,899 --> 00:40:42,715
It's because they have live ammo.

624
00:40:45,240 --> 00:40:49,397
I think I saw a soldier shooting live ammo at the GOP in a drama.

625
00:40:49,397 --> 00:40:51,812
I saw that drama too.

626
00:40:53,409 --> 00:40:54,980
He looks a bit like you.

627
00:40:54,980 --> 00:40:58,003
No, I'm much slimmer.

628
00:40:58,003 --> 00:41:00,020
Is that so?

629
00:41:00,020 --> 00:41:03,961
Anyway, you have a lot of amazing experiences at the GOP.

630
00:41:03,961 --> 00:41:06,360
You'll be on duty like this,

631
00:41:06,360 --> 00:41:09,480
and you'll think it's a bird, but it's a moth.

632
00:41:09,480 --> 00:41:12,620
You'll think it's a real bird, but it's a mosquito.

633
00:41:12,620 --> 00:41:16,420
A fighter jet zooms by, but it's an eagle.

634
00:41:16,420 --> 00:41:20,249
You'll wonder why a tank is there, but it's a wild boar.

635
00:41:20,249 --> 00:41:24,700
It's crazy. I heard it's a completely different world.

636
00:41:24,700 --> 00:41:26,840
But isn't that a bit of a stretch?

637
00:41:26,840 --> 00:41:29,907
True. There's probably some exaggeration.

638
00:41:29,907 --> 00:41:33,194
Guys come back from the GOP and brag about their military service,

639
00:41:33,194 --> 00:41:37,440
saying it was tough, just to have drinking stories for life.

640
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:41,213
But the GOP must have way too many shifts.

641
00:41:41,213 --> 00:41:46,220
Once you're in, it's for six months or a year. North Korea is right there too.

642
00:41:46,220 --> 00:41:48,100
Winter is no joke there.

643
00:41:48,100 --> 00:41:51,411
Plus, you can't go out, take overnight leave, or have visitors.

644
00:41:51,411 --> 00:41:54,541
I think it would be so lonely.

645
00:41:55,380 --> 00:42:01,169
Then why don't we all put the same thing for our first to third choices?

646
00:42:02,022 --> 00:42:03,899
Sounds good.

647
00:42:03,899 --> 00:42:06,652
We're all putting the same thing?

648
00:42:07,720 --> 00:42:12,620
Wouldn't it be better to go together than with a bunch of strangers?

649
00:42:12,620 --> 00:42:16,803
- That's true. - Right. I'm definitely going with you guys.

650
00:42:21,083 --> 00:42:23,908
Your face is saying otherwise.

651
00:42:23,908 --> 00:42:27,900
No, I'm just really thinking about which would be best.

652
00:42:27,900 --> 00:42:34,153
It's like we're in hell, but deciding which hell to go to.

653
00:42:35,681 --> 00:42:39,472
Are we really all checking "remain at unit?"

654
00:42:39,472 --> 00:42:42,932
Competition will be fierce, but let's do that for now.

655
00:42:42,932 --> 00:42:44,032
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

656
00:42:44,032 --> 00:42:47,470
- No betrayals, everyone. - Yes, sir.

657
00:43:02,472 --> 00:43:05,400
- Did you get the forms from the guys? - Yes, sir.

658
00:43:05,400 --> 00:43:07,292
Let's see.

659
00:43:11,127 --> 00:43:16,096
Dong Woo, remain. Jeong Min, remain.

660
00:43:16,096 --> 00:43:19,683
Byeong Ho, remain. Jeon Se Gye, remain.

661
00:43:19,683 --> 00:43:24,032
- All of Barracks 3 are staying. Barracks 1? - Here it is.

662
00:43:24,032 --> 00:43:26,272
Sang Hun, remain.

663
00:43:26,272 --> 00:43:29,776
Da Hye... Air Defense Brigade?

664
00:43:29,776 --> 00:43:32,821
Park Min Seok. What? GOP.

665
00:43:32,821 --> 00:43:35,445
Moon Bit Na Ri is also GOP.

666
00:43:35,445 --> 00:43:39,192
Hyeon Uk, remain. Did these guys have a fight?

667
00:43:39,192 --> 00:43:41,912
- I'm not sure. - What about you guys?

668
00:43:41,912 --> 00:43:45,192
- We're going to follow the first sergeant. - Yes, that's right.

669
00:43:45,192 --> 00:43:46,332
Where's he going?

670
00:43:46,332 --> 00:43:49,372
I'm not sure. What about you, Assistant Platoon Leader?

671
00:43:49,372 --> 00:43:52,392
I don't know. I'll just go where I'm told.

672
00:43:52,392 --> 00:43:54,752
You guys are going through a lot because of this.

673
00:43:54,752 --> 00:43:59,632
Ever since Major Kim Ha Na arrived, our workload has increased tremendously.

674
00:43:59,632 --> 00:44:04,684
We used to just do our jobs, but now it's "do this, do that." It's a total nightmare.

675
00:44:04,684 --> 00:44:09,147
She makes us check every single thing from one end of the base to the other.

676
00:44:12,653 --> 00:44:18,781
She's so detailed and meticulous that there's really a lot to learn from her.

677
00:44:18,781 --> 00:44:21,195
So much to learn...

678
00:44:23,703 --> 00:44:26,792
Chungseong! Love you! Respectful Major Kim Ha Na!

679
00:44:26,792 --> 00:44:31,246
What did the clerks do to deserve this hell?

680
00:44:31,246 --> 00:44:33,032
Well...

681
00:44:33,032 --> 00:44:37,212
You got wits, though. Pulling a U-turn and starting to brown-nose.

682
00:44:37,212 --> 00:44:40,217
My most sincere words always come out last.

683
00:44:40,217 --> 00:44:43,606
Hurry up and organize the equipment handover data and the personnel list.

684
00:44:43,606 --> 00:44:46,383
- Yes, ma'am. - Good.

685
00:44:50,607 --> 00:44:53,182
So, are you guys doing a good job?

686
00:44:55,237 --> 00:44:58,946
- Sung Yoon Mo? - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

687
00:44:58,946 --> 00:45:02,162
I assume Corporal No is treating you well?

688
00:45:02,162 --> 00:45:04,169
Yes, ma'am.

689
00:45:04,169 --> 00:45:09,501
He's very meticulous and teaches me everything one by one. He's great.

690
00:45:09,501 --> 00:45:13,839
- Is that so? - Corporal No Hee Jeong. That's right.

691
00:45:13,839 --> 00:45:16,384
It looks like he treats you well.

692
00:45:17,968 --> 00:45:23,348
But is Corporal No quick-witted or not?

693
00:45:23,348 --> 00:45:26,489
- I'm not sure what you mean... - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

694
00:45:26,489 --> 00:45:27,728
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

695
00:45:27,728 --> 00:45:34,359
Can you bring me the facility inspection log and the corrective action log?

696
00:45:34,359 --> 00:45:36,352
Yes, ma'am.

697
00:45:39,792 --> 00:45:42,453
- I'll do it. - Yes.

698
00:45:47,932 --> 00:45:49,892
- Good work. - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

699
00:45:49,892 --> 00:45:51,734
- Take care, ma'am. - Are you heading out?

700
00:45:51,734 --> 00:45:52,632
No.

701
00:45:52,632 --> 00:45:56,044
- Yes, ma'am. - Take care, ma'am. Chungseong! Love you!

702
00:46:01,345 --> 00:46:05,432
- Did you just flip me off? - No, ma'am. This is also a misunderstanding.

703
00:46:05,432 --> 00:46:07,798
- Is it? - Yes.

704
00:46:10,072 --> 00:46:13,192
- You have something on you here. - Where? Here?

705
00:46:13,192 --> 00:46:15,039
Right here, here.

706
00:46:17,855 --> 00:46:19,952
I've had it. Let's cut it off.

707
00:46:19,952 --> 00:46:22,872
Wait, no! This is also a misunderstanding. Seriously!

708
00:46:22,872 --> 00:46:25,696
- No, I have to cut this off. - It's a misunderstanding! Really, no!

709
00:46:25,696 --> 00:46:29,451
"No Hee Jeong is a total idiot."

710
00:46:29,451 --> 00:46:32,528
"Agreed. I feel you."

711
00:46:34,002 --> 00:46:36,192
Major Kim Ha Na is the best.

712
00:46:36,192 --> 00:46:40,367
- Just once, please! - Come here!

713
00:46:41,352 --> 00:46:44,488
I was planning to buy each company a meal for their hard work...

714
00:46:44,488 --> 00:46:48,119
But for this company, it happened to fall on today.

715
00:46:48,992 --> 00:46:50,558
Thank you.

716
00:46:51,895 --> 00:46:53,441
Here.

717
00:46:54,611 --> 00:46:57,572
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu. Thank you.

718
00:47:01,232 --> 00:47:02,752
- Thank you. - You're welcome.

719
00:47:02,752 --> 00:47:07,200
I haven't been in the service for long,

720
00:47:07,992 --> 00:47:12,292
but now that I'm here, I've experienced so many things.

721
00:47:12,292 --> 00:47:15,379
I think it'll be very memorable.

722
00:47:15,379 --> 00:47:18,143
In a good way or a bad way?

723
00:47:21,008 --> 00:47:23,594
Half and half.

724
00:47:23,594 --> 00:47:26,272
Battalion Commander, you seem to have changed a bit too.

725
00:47:26,272 --> 00:47:29,755
- In a good way or a bad way? - Half and half.

726
00:47:32,632 --> 00:47:37,980
Well, it was a short time, but I was really happy thanks to this company.

727
00:47:37,980 --> 00:47:40,152
- Let's have a drink. - Yes, sir.

728
00:47:40,152 --> 00:47:42,208
- Thank you. - Thank you.

729
00:47:46,592 --> 00:47:49,192
With our Second Company Commander...

730
00:47:49,192 --> 00:47:51,496
so much has happened.

731
00:47:51,496 --> 00:47:53,832
You've had a hard time because of me.

732
00:47:53,832 --> 00:47:58,432
Not at all. I've learned more.

733
00:47:58,432 --> 00:48:03,592
I may be higher in rank, but I've learned a lot. Especially...

734
00:48:03,592 --> 00:48:05,672
things like jokes.

735
00:48:05,672 --> 00:48:08,472
You should've learned jokes from me, not the company commander.

736
00:48:08,472 --> 00:48:10,812
Exactly.

737
00:48:10,812 --> 00:48:12,904
I don't think that's right.

738
00:48:14,732 --> 00:48:16,855
- First Sergeant. - Yes?

739
00:48:16,855 --> 00:48:19,009
You must be very sad.

740
00:48:19,812 --> 00:48:21,312
Well, I suppose so.

741
00:48:21,312 --> 00:48:24,472
I spent my entire youth here.

742
00:48:24,472 --> 00:48:28,952
First Sergeant, have you been stationed here for over 20 years?

743
00:48:28,952 --> 00:48:30,631
Something like that.

744
00:48:30,631 --> 00:48:33,512
Has it already been that long?

745
00:48:33,512 --> 00:48:37,515
I've seen off soldiers and officers,

746
00:48:40,128 --> 00:48:42,546
and now I'm seeing off the unit itself.

747
00:48:46,288 --> 00:48:50,348
Then will you stay here until the end?

748
00:48:50,348 --> 00:48:54,140
Yes. My youth is buried here.

749
00:48:54,140 --> 00:48:56,412
I have to watch over it until the end.

750
00:49:02,768 --> 00:49:04,581
Come in.

751
00:49:09,908 --> 00:49:11,658
Come in.

752
00:49:17,457 --> 00:49:19,143
Chungseong!

753
00:49:21,348 --> 00:49:23,651
I asked her to come.

754
00:49:25,424 --> 00:49:29,348
You could at least pretend to be happy. You guys look so unwelcoming.

755
00:49:29,348 --> 00:49:32,565
Right. Come over here.

756
00:49:33,816 --> 00:49:36,179
Excuse me.

757
00:49:36,179 --> 00:49:39,045
She's here on dispatch, but still,

758
00:49:39,045 --> 00:49:44,026
since she's at our unit, I thought it'd be nice of her to join us.

759
00:49:44,026 --> 00:49:47,788
You heard that, right? I was invited too.

760
00:49:47,788 --> 00:49:49,968
- Do you drink? - Yes.

761
00:49:49,968 --> 00:49:51,664
Here you go.

762
00:49:58,508 --> 00:50:02,875
I've visited many different units while conducting inspections,

763
00:50:02,875 --> 00:50:05,422
but this place seems a bit different.

764
00:50:05,422 --> 00:50:09,828
It has a strong scent.

765
00:50:09,828 --> 00:50:13,514
It has a strong scent of humanity.

766
00:50:13,514 --> 00:50:18,008
It's a rare scent to find in the military, but I liked it.

767
00:50:18,008 --> 00:50:21,508
- Is that a compliment? - That's a bit ambiguous.

768
00:50:21,508 --> 00:50:23,648
It's a compliment.

769
00:50:23,648 --> 00:50:25,564
All thanks to the battalion commander.

770
00:50:25,564 --> 00:50:28,108
I just happened to be assigned to a good place.

771
00:50:28,108 --> 00:50:31,073
I've been both an enlisted soldier and an NCO,

772
00:50:31,073 --> 00:50:35,268
but I know the first sergeant always works the hardest.

773
00:50:35,268 --> 00:50:38,128
Listen to this guy talking nonsense.

774
00:50:38,128 --> 00:50:43,662
I wish I could spend more time with such great people. It's a shame.

775
00:50:48,067 --> 00:50:52,369
Let's have a toast to the day we meet again somewhere.

776
00:50:52,369 --> 00:50:53,384
Yes, sir.

777
00:50:53,384 --> 00:50:57,410
Hey, Ddong Il Gu, why don't you give us a toast?

778
00:50:57,410 --> 00:50:59,408
How can I toast before you, First Sergeant?

779
00:50:59,408 --> 00:51:03,542
I'm really looking forward to it, Staff Sergeant Choi.

780
00:51:03,542 --> 00:51:04,808
I'm not good at this.

781
00:51:04,808 --> 00:51:07,528
You know our Ddong Il Gu. It'll be worth it.

782
00:51:07,528 --> 00:51:10,408
- First Sergeant, I can't. - Choi Il Gu, do it or go to the brig.

783
00:51:10,408 --> 00:51:13,348
- Company Commander, I really can't. - Il Gu.

784
00:51:13,348 --> 00:51:15,589
- Yes? - I believe in you.

785
00:51:16,768 --> 00:51:22,668
Since even the battalion commander said so, I'll do my absolute best.

786
00:51:22,668 --> 00:51:24,917
- Right. - Go ahead.

787
00:51:26,712 --> 00:51:30,981
I'll do an acrostic poem using the name "Choi Il Gu."

788
00:51:32,551 --> 00:51:34,763
- Choi! - Choi!

789
00:51:34,763 --> 00:51:37,321
Choi go (The best) officers...

790
00:51:45,772 --> 00:51:48,045
It was an honor...

791
00:51:48,981 --> 00:51:51,175
to be with you all.

792
00:51:52,985 --> 00:51:54,752
- Il! - Il!

793
00:51:55,866 --> 00:51:58,868
Il bu ro (On purpose), I'm not tearing up.

794
00:51:58,868 --> 00:52:01,093
When I think about it,

795
00:52:02,080 --> 00:52:07,711
you always put the soldiers first, like a father, like a mother...

796
00:52:07,711 --> 00:52:10,178
and like an older brother or sister.

797
00:52:10,178 --> 00:52:13,988
Thanks to you, I'm finishing my service...

798
00:52:13,988 --> 00:52:18,847
with a healthy body and great memories of the military. Truly...

799
00:52:18,847 --> 00:52:21,268
Truly, thank you.

800
00:52:21,268 --> 00:52:24,928
The last thing I want to say is...

801
00:52:24,928 --> 00:52:26,687
- Gu! - Gu!

802
00:52:28,228 --> 00:52:31,962
- It's not "Gu ra" (a lie), is it? - How did you...

803
00:52:31,962 --> 00:52:35,113
Battalion Commander, Il Gu has too much seniority for that.

804
00:52:35,113 --> 00:52:38,588
Our Ddong Il Gu isn't that out of touch.

805
00:52:38,588 --> 00:52:40,874
I have high expectations.

806
00:52:43,455 --> 00:52:47,149
I'm sorry. It is 'Gu ra' (a lie).

807
00:52:49,753 --> 00:52:53,308
But I still love you all!

808
00:52:53,308 --> 00:52:56,827
- Right, we love you too. - Love you!

809
00:52:56,827 --> 00:52:59,904
Thank you. Thank you.

810
00:53:01,827 --> 00:53:04,308
- So? Are we all done? - Yes.

811
00:53:04,308 --> 00:53:07,368
- Shall we head out then? - Yes, let's go.

812
00:53:07,368 --> 00:53:09,571
What kind of toast was that?

813
00:53:09,571 --> 00:53:13,718
You need to relearn how to joke. Follow me, you punk.

814
00:53:14,733 --> 00:53:17,391
- Captain Cho Baek Ho? - Yes.

815
00:53:18,112 --> 00:53:20,492
How have you been?

816
00:53:20,492 --> 00:53:22,069
Good, ma'am.

817
00:53:25,288 --> 00:53:28,038
Is the second round at the chicken place?

818
00:53:29,376 --> 00:53:32,761
Look who's here.

819
00:53:54,148 --> 00:53:55,608
Aren't you going to work?

820
00:53:55,608 --> 00:54:00,108
Come on, man, I'm the second most senior here. I need to rest.

821
00:54:00,108 --> 00:54:04,448
But why are we pulling weeds when the unit is being disbanded?

822
00:54:04,448 --> 00:54:06,284
That's the military for you, man.

823
00:54:06,284 --> 00:54:10,180
The officers will keep making us work until the unit is officially gone.

824
00:54:14,028 --> 00:54:19,974
But it's so sad to think I won't be discharged from here.

825
00:54:20,928 --> 00:54:24,268
I never imagined it would really disappear.

826
00:54:24,268 --> 00:54:29,148
It was a total mess when Min Seok first arrived here, right?

827
00:54:29,148 --> 00:54:31,008
How was it?

828
00:54:31,008 --> 00:54:34,408
The unit went crazy because the division commander's son arrived.

829
00:54:34,408 --> 00:54:37,788
Hey, Min Sik!

830
00:54:37,788 --> 00:54:39,988
It's Min Seok. Hey.

831
00:54:39,988 --> 00:54:43,033
I thought this was where I'd stay until my discharge.

832
00:54:43,033 --> 00:54:46,125
What? You'll be discharged from here?

833
00:54:46,912 --> 00:54:48,516
Shouldn't I be?

834
00:54:48,516 --> 00:54:50,911
No way.

835
00:54:52,372 --> 00:54:57,552
But come to think of it, everything felt so unfamiliar when I first came.

836
00:54:57,552 --> 00:54:58,932
- New recruit here? - He's here.

837
00:54:58,932 --> 00:55:03,071
- Chungseong! - Unpack his gear and feed him.

838
00:55:03,812 --> 00:55:06,872
Now, I'm so used to everything.

839
00:55:06,872 --> 00:55:08,304
The guardhouse...

840
00:55:08,304 --> 00:55:11,812
- Halt! Hands up! Move and I'll shoot! - Go ahead and shoot!

841
00:55:11,812 --> 00:55:12,892
The smoking area...

842
00:55:12,892 --> 00:55:16,441
Let's make a lot of good memories while we're here.

843
00:55:16,441 --> 00:55:19,528
The laundry drying area, and where we polished our boots.

844
00:55:19,528 --> 00:55:22,438
Hello? Everyone?

845
00:55:22,438 --> 00:55:23,512
I'm sorry.

846
00:55:23,512 --> 00:55:25,397
Corporal Park Min Seok reporting to the admin office.

847
00:55:25,397 --> 00:55:26,632
The admin office, too.

848
00:55:26,632 --> 00:55:31,337
- Shut up! - Put Il Gu in the middle and grab him!

849
00:55:31,337 --> 00:55:35,346
- The barracks... - Not much longer. Hang in there.

850
00:55:40,752 --> 00:55:45,240
A bird that looks like a sparrow has appeared at one o'clock.

851
00:55:51,268 --> 00:55:53,536
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

852
00:55:53,536 --> 00:55:56,021
Chungseong! Love you! Congrats on your discharge!

853
00:55:56,021 --> 00:55:57,674
- Chungseong! - Chungseong!

854
00:55:57,674 --> 00:55:59,412
[Building an Elite Regiment That Fights and Wins]

855
00:55:59,412 --> 00:56:01,081
Park Min Seok.

856
00:56:02,066 --> 00:56:04,675
- Private First Class Park Min Seok. - Look over there.

857
00:56:06,113 --> 00:56:07,588
The unit.

858
00:56:08,554 --> 00:56:12,976
The unit? It's the unit! It's our unit!

859
00:56:16,532 --> 00:56:20,147
There isn't a single spot that doesn't hold a memory.

860
00:56:27,112 --> 00:56:29,558
I've finally gotten used to it...

861
00:56:31,225 --> 00:56:34,091
But now I have to leave.

862
00:56:35,592 --> 00:56:37,499
It feels strange.

863
00:56:38,152 --> 00:56:40,150
The new recruits are here!

864
00:56:41,112 --> 00:56:44,012
Really? That's crazy.

865
00:56:44,012 --> 00:56:46,647
- There are new recruits. - New recruits!

866
00:56:48,292 --> 00:56:52,312
Why send new recruits when the unit is being consolidated?

867
00:56:52,312 --> 00:56:55,886
- That's the military for you. - What do you know, you punk?

868
00:57:07,778 --> 00:57:10,320
Chungseong! Love you. New recruits?

869
00:57:10,320 --> 00:57:12,172
- Can't you tell? - Can't you tell?

870
00:57:12,172 --> 00:57:13,892
- Don't copy me. - Yes, sir.

871
00:57:13,892 --> 00:57:16,852
- The new recruits are here! - There are three of them!

872
00:57:16,852 --> 00:57:21,372
- Three of them? - Hyeon Uk is so lucky. Seriously.

873
00:57:21,372 --> 00:57:23,872
Private Kim Hyeon Uk. No, sir. Thank you.

874
00:57:23,872 --> 00:57:26,443
- Bit Na Ri is lucky too. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

875
00:57:26,443 --> 00:57:27,612
I'm happy, sir.

876
00:57:27,612 --> 00:57:30,290
- Let's go see them. - Let's go.

877
00:57:31,452 --> 00:57:33,992
- Recruits, attention. - Attention!

878
00:57:33,992 --> 00:57:36,790
From now on, the Second Company is your home.

879
00:57:36,790 --> 00:57:39,251
Think of it as your own home.

880
00:57:39,251 --> 00:57:42,454
If there's anything you don't know, ask the officers or seniors here.

881
00:57:42,454 --> 00:57:44,592
- Got it? - Yes, sir!

882
00:57:44,592 --> 00:57:48,432
Alright, I'll go get the platoon roster, so look after the boys.

883
00:57:48,432 --> 00:57:51,332
- Yes, sir. - And Ddong Il Gu.

884
00:57:51,332 --> 00:57:53,612
- Yes? - Don't pick on the new guys, okay?

885
00:57:53,612 --> 00:57:57,492
First Sergeant, I'm an NCO now. I don't do such childish things.

886
00:57:57,492 --> 00:57:59,029
I'll keep a close eye on him.

887
00:57:59,029 --> 00:58:01,064
You're the same, you punk.

888
00:58:01,064 --> 00:58:04,662
- Wait here. - Yes, Chungseong! Love you!

889
00:58:07,905 --> 00:58:11,366
- These faces scream "ace." - Yes, sir.

890
00:58:11,366 --> 00:58:14,091
Let's see.

891
00:58:14,091 --> 00:58:16,952
- Min Ho. - Private Seo Min Ho.

892
00:58:16,952 --> 00:58:19,830
Good voice, Min Ho.

893
00:58:19,830 --> 00:58:21,623
Inje, Gangwon-do?

894
00:58:21,623 --> 00:58:26,443
Cheonryeongsan Chilseong? Is this right?

895
00:58:26,443 --> 00:58:27,716
Yes, that is correct.

896
00:58:27,716 --> 00:58:30,272
- Did you come from the mountains? - Yes, I did.

897
00:58:30,272 --> 00:58:33,505
- The reason is at the bottom... - The bottom?

898
00:58:34,246 --> 00:58:37,752
- Shamanic initiation? You were initiated? - Yes, that is correct.

899
00:58:37,752 --> 00:58:40,852
No wonder I got the chills.

900
00:58:40,852 --> 00:58:44,207
Then do you actually see things... like ghosts?

901
00:58:44,207 --> 00:58:46,132
You crazy bastard, why would you ask that?

902
00:58:46,132 --> 00:58:50,215
Aren't you curious? Answer quietly.

903
00:58:50,215 --> 00:58:53,283
- Okay. - Scary.

904
00:58:53,283 --> 00:58:57,709
Then are there any ghosts here right now?

905
00:58:57,709 --> 00:58:59,336
Take a look.

906
00:59:03,343 --> 00:59:05,945
- He's doing it. - What's with him?

907
00:59:05,945 --> 00:59:07,913
He's rolling it.

908
00:59:16,868 --> 00:59:19,817
His gaze has changed.

909
00:59:19,817 --> 00:59:23,010
Something's here.

910
00:59:23,812 --> 00:59:25,657
Not yet.

911
00:59:36,415 --> 00:59:40,692
That's where the clerk hanged himself a long time ago. Right there!

912
00:59:40,692 --> 00:59:43,264
Hey, I always got so sleepy on duty there!

913
00:59:43,264 --> 00:59:47,070
Exactly! Whenever I was on duty, the back of my neck would get so stiff.

914
00:59:48,839 --> 00:59:53,792
- Stop lying. - You're just a rookie. You don't know.

915
00:59:53,792 --> 00:59:58,136
So, what kind of god do you serve?

916
00:59:58,136 --> 01:00:00,126
I serve a child spirit.

917
01:00:00,126 --> 01:00:04,448
We didn't get a new recruit, we got a possessed recruit.

918
01:00:04,448 --> 01:00:08,147
Enough, enough. Put that away now.

919
01:00:08,147 --> 01:00:09,152
Yes, sir.

920
01:00:09,152 --> 01:00:13,382
- The guy next to him is no joke either. - What is it?

921
01:00:13,382 --> 01:00:15,208
What about him?

922
01:00:16,692 --> 01:00:20,237
- Lee Jae Ho. - Private Lee Jae Ho.

923
01:00:21,132 --> 01:00:27,085
What? Spero Brooke School, Haute Rosemary Union University?

924
01:00:27,085 --> 01:00:30,352
Wow. These are all in the US. You must be good at English.

925
01:00:30,352 --> 01:00:35,332
Can you do something like introducing yourself in English?

926
01:00:36,052 --> 01:00:39,776
Yes, Staff Sergeant. I was studying at Cornell, but I put school on hold.

927
01:00:39,776 --> 01:00:44,391
My dad used to tell me that no one is fit to be a leader in the company,

928
01:00:44,391 --> 01:00:46,574
unless they've been humbled in the military.

929
01:00:46,574 --> 01:00:49,733
I'll never forget that. If I can't serve my country,

930
01:00:49,733 --> 01:00:53,152
I don't think I deserve to be a leader. That's the reason I enlisted...

931
01:00:53,152 --> 01:00:57,612
Okay, stop. I didn't ask you to give such a long speech.

932
01:00:57,612 --> 01:00:59,628
Hey, I'll explain it to you later.

933
01:00:59,628 --> 01:01:01,836
I got it.

934
01:01:01,836 --> 01:01:05,156
Foreign citizenship. You could've skipped service. Why'd you come?

935
01:01:05,156 --> 01:01:09,165
My father said I must serve in the military.

936
01:01:09,165 --> 01:01:11,316
Good father.

937
01:01:11,316 --> 01:01:14,256
Your father is...

938
01:01:14,256 --> 01:01:18,216
Chairman of Samhan JoongAng Group... Hey, that's a top-tier conglomerate.

939
01:01:18,216 --> 01:01:20,296
Yes, that is correct.

940
01:01:20,296 --> 01:01:22,656
This is insane.

941
01:01:22,656 --> 01:01:27,811
- And the guy next to him is amazing too. - What about him?

942
01:01:28,556 --> 01:01:31,807
I'm almost scared to turn the page.

943
01:01:31,807 --> 01:01:35,191
- Oh Seung Hyeon. - Private Oh Seung Hyeon.

944
01:01:35,191 --> 01:01:37,211
Nothing unusual here?

945
01:01:37,211 --> 01:01:39,996
[National Team Reserve]

946
01:01:39,996 --> 01:01:42,976
- You're on the national reserve team? - Yes, that is correct.

947
01:01:42,976 --> 01:01:46,456
- I've never seen a national athlete. - I know, right?

948
01:01:46,456 --> 01:01:48,475
- What's your sport? - New recruit?

949
01:01:48,475 --> 01:01:50,510
Yes, sir.

950
01:01:53,338 --> 01:01:55,659
- Hey. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

951
01:01:55,659 --> 01:01:57,526
- You happy? - No, sir.

952
01:01:57,526 --> 01:02:00,015
- Don't smirk. - Sorry, sir.

953
01:02:02,456 --> 01:02:03,720
New recruits!

954
01:02:03,720 --> 01:02:07,157
- Private Seo Min Ho. - Private Lee Jae Ho! Private Oh Seung Hyeon!

955
01:02:07,157 --> 01:02:10,896
- Let's get along. - Yes, sir!

956
01:02:10,896 --> 01:02:13,088
Things are about to get interesting.

957
01:02:38,556 --> 01:02:42,416
[We Were All Someone's New Recruit Once]
